From 5e49479660677e0fe6b7e020332b600161874dc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sachin <sachinbarange86@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:23:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stamp POCO F7 instead of REDMI Turbo 4 Pro

The watermark plugin asks the device config class for a {brand, model} pair and prints it verbatim; Lonyx; inherits the codename the dump came from. This is not ro.product.marketname, so no prop can fix it. The class resolves on ro.product.device=onyx, which is this phone, so the pair becomes POCO / F7.

Signed-off-by: Sachin <sachinbarange86@gmail.com>
---
 smali_classes3/onyx.smali | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/smali_classes3/onyx.smali b/smali_classes3/onyx.smali
index 4375447f..f242c547 100644
--- a/smali_classes3/onyx.smali
+++ b/smali_classes3/onyx.smali
@@ -499,9 +499,9 @@
 
     invoke-direct {p0, v0}, Landroid/util/SparseArray;-><init>(I)V
 
-    const-string v0, "REDMI"
+    const-string v0, "POCO"
 
-    const-string v1, "Turbo 4 Pro"
+    const-string v1, "F7"
 
     filled-new-array {v0, v1}, [Ljava/lang/String;
 
-- 
2.43.0

